claims.description:
Let the owner's confirmation follow the diff, behind the protected local_review.confirmation with value "diff", valid only together with local_review.binding "diff". Absent means a confirmation names the exact head, byte-identical to today (proven by tests). With the setting, an /approve-intent comment or an approving review of an earlier commit S also counts for the current head H when all of these hold:
- S is an ancestor of H;
- the normalized diff of S from its merge base with the live base equals the pull request's current normalized diff (receipt-patch.cjs canonicalHunks/diffDigest);
- S's merge base carries the same .github/clouseau.json and repository_policy contract as the live base.
Fail closed: any diff change, another lineage, an unknown commit, a patchless or truncated file list (300+ files or a count different from changed_files), a non-maintainer or a bot never match; any other API failure surfaces. The comment stays exactly "/approve-intent <sha>" at the gate. Apply it in purposeConfirmation, maintainerConfirmed, reassess and the gate's issue_comment check. The recorded authorization keeps head_sha and adds confirmed_sha only when it differs.
Tests name five branch-update cases for both the diff-bound receipt and the confirmation:
(a) a merge of main with unrelated files keeps both;
(b) a rebase onto the new main keeps the receipt but voids the confirmation in this PR, because the ancestry check cannot see a rebased commit. Carrying it across a rebase is a separate follow-up;
(c) a clean merge where main changed the same file only shifts hunk offsets and keeps both, but an edit inside the branch hunk's context lines voids both;
(d) a new commit voids both;
(e) a conflict resolution that alters the branch's own lines voids both.
Docs updated. The owner decided this (relayed by the orchestrating session). It lands dark and is enabled only by a later config change.

